["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"service-sdk","stream_identity":"01a0d3a0-375d-7500-8fe2-64f501bcf4bb","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"story","fields":{"body":"# Version live parent authority and executable service scenarios\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A new `sdk.derive.inherit-parent-authority/v2` provider preserves the frozen v1 meaning and derives child projection owner/scopes from the current folded parent.\n- Parent transfer cannot leave stale child visibility; engine tests prove the former owner value is replaced.\n- Generated Connector factories accept a deployment-injected authenticated authority-facts resolver while retaining a safe principal/group default.\n- The resolver receives only receiver-verified principal context; tenant, realm, authority, user, and executor remain absent from operation inputs.\n- service-builder emits generated Rust conformance tests for every declared scenario fixture.\n- The conformance runner invokes intents and queries through the generated Connector factory and proves exact `None` versus `Some(\"default\")` partition authority.\n- Existing deterministic generation, cross-artifact conformance, runtime, documentation, and AEP gates pass.\n","document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-aa7232af547dbc9b4b01d65a0b9633c6","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/live-parent-authority-conformance","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Version live parent authority and executable service scenarios\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A new `sdk.derive.inherit-parent-authority/v2` provider preserves the frozen v1 meaning and derives child projection owner/scopes from the current folded parent.\n- Parent transfer cannot leave stale child visibility; engine tests prove the former owner value is replaced.\n- Generated Connector factories accept a deployment-injected authenticated authority-facts resolver while retaining a safe principal/group default.\n- The resolver receives only receiver-verified principal context; tenant, realm, authority, user, and executor remain absent from operation inputs.\n- service-builder emits generated Rust conformance tests for every declared scenario fixture.\n- The conformance runner invokes intents and queries through the generated Connector factory and proves exact `None` versus `Some(\"default\")` partition authority.\n- Existing deterministic generation, cross-artifact conformance, runtime, documentation, and AEP gates pass.\n","relations":[{"derived_from":"epic:builder-runtime"},{"serves":"vision:composable-services"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Add a v2 inherited-authority obligation, injected auth facts, and generated Connector scenario execution.","title":"Version live parent authority and executable service scenarios"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"},"relations":[{"derived_from":"epic:builder-runtime"},{"serves":"vision:composable-services"}],"summary":"Add a v2 inherited-authority obligation, injected auth facts, and generated Connector scenario execution.","title":"Version live parent authority and executable service scenarios"},"id":"ent-aa7232af547dbc9b4b01d65a0b9633c6","lifecycle_state":"implemented","revision":4,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["story","ent-aa7232af547dbc9b4b01d65a0b9633c6"]}]